{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall turn back and encamp before Pi-hahiroth.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, commanded that they turn back behind them, toward Egypt, before Pi-hahiroth — that is, Pithom; and it is called Hairoth because there Israel were made free men. And He further added to say, <b>before Baal-zephon.</b> And all these matters are causes in that his heart will be strengthened, as it is written: וחזקתי את לב פרעה ורדף אחריהם. And the parashah will explain by means of this three causes: the first is what is written, ללכת יומם ולילה — in order that they think that they are fleeing, as I have explained; the second is what is written, וישובו ויחנו — He commanded them to turn back behind them so that Pharaoh would say on account of this, 'the children of Israel are entangled in the land,' and therefore they are turning back toward Egypt; and the third is what is written, לפני בעל צפון — He commanded them to establish camp before Baal-zephon, and it was an idol, like (II Kings 1:3–4) בעל זבוב אלהי עקרון, and likewise בעל פעור; and it — it alone — was what remained of all the gods of Egypt, upon which the plagues had been executed on the night of the smiting of the firstborn. And the matter was in order to mislead them, in the manner of what is said (Job 12:23): ״משגיא לגוים ויאבדם״. And it says <b>opposite it you shall encamp by the sea,</b> that is, opposite Baal-zephon; and therefore Pharaoh said, סגר עליהם המדבר — that is, by the power of Baal-zephon. And there is here an allusion in the verse, from what they saw upon the sea."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:48.464070211Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}